  "notes": "Alt-pop swinging between electropop concept-album and industrial/alt-rock, encoded on the straight class the entry names for all three modes. The drum grammar is the entry's own: \"electropop mode uses programmed trap-lite kick/clap with 16th hats; the Reznor/Ross-produced mode uses distorted machine drums, industrial noise hits and no swing.\" \"No swing\" is authored literally as a hard-quantised humanize block — `quantizeStrength` 0.98 and the lowest `velocityVar` in this section — and the \"industrial noise hits\" are the `impact` and `riser` perc lanes, which no other model in this batch uses. The 808 is authored because the entry names it — \"808 and distorted synth sub in the pop mode; fuzz bass guitar in the rock mode. Bass is used for weight, not counterline\" — as `counter_riff` at `heavy` distortion, and that \"weight, not counterline\" is why the bassline sits at `followRootsProb` 0.96 on a kick mirror with almost no passing motion. Harmony is \"4-bar minor loops\" with \"modal (Aeolian/Dorian) inflection\", which is the scale weighting and the minor families. Melody encodes \"narrow-range and rhythmically clipped with the hook sung on repeated notes\" as a two-to-four-pitch motif, a staccato articulation and a `riff_loop` structure; \"harmony vocals are used as texture blocks\" is the `sustain_pad` counter. Arrangement encodes the documented device of putting the drop-out *inside* the chorus. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says so — \"per-album genre turns, producers and vocal character documented; tempo/harmony bands inferred\" — and every drum probability, the humanize numbers and the harmonic bands here are INFERRED for the same reason. `bpm.mode` 105 is the midpoint of the stated 90—120 pop core.",
